+`orders.daily_total.anomaly` (warn) compares yesterday's order total, per currency, with the
+mean daily total of the 28 days before it; days are calendar days in `REPORTING_ZONE`, and
+cancelled orders are left out, as in the daily sales report. A total more than
+`ANOMALY_FACTOR` times above or below the mean fails the check (a day without orders in a
+currency that had them counts as 0). The mean is taken over the days that had orders; a
+currency with fewer than 7 such days has no baseline yet and passes. Details give each
+currency outside the range with its total as a multiple of the mean.
+
 **Reports.** Days are calendar days in `REPORTING_ZONE`, so an order placed at 23:30 UTC in
 summer belongs to the next day in Berlin, and the day of a DST change has 23 or 25 hours.
 
